    {
      "id": "8x2ptf6",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4.1 Introduction to Plant Pathology"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Plant pathology studies plant diseases, their etiology, disease cycles, and management strategies.",
        "Disease manifestation requires three essential elements of the Disease Triangle: a susceptible host, a virulent pathogen, and a favorable environment.",
        "Fungi are responsible for the vast majority of plant diseases, followed by bacteria, viruses, phytoplasmas, and nematodes.",
        "Plant disease management relies on five general principles: avoidance, exclusion, eradication, protection, and host resistance.",
        "Integrated Disease Management (IDM) optimizes chemical, biological, physical, and cultural practices to minimize economic loss."
      ],
      "id": "1xfyra8"
    },
