    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Anton de Bary is known as the Father of Plant Pathology, whereas E.J. Butler is recognized as the Father of Indian Plant Pathology.",
        "Late blight of potato is caused by Phytophthora infestans, the organism responsible for the Great Irish Famine of 1845.",
        "Bordeaux mixture is composed of Copper Sulfate, Lime, and Water (1:1:100 ratio) and was discovered by P.M.A. Millardet in 1882.",
        "Karnal bunt of wheat is caused by Tilletia indica and carries major sanitary and phytosanitary quarantine significance."
      ],
      "id": "gw70jx2"
    },
